# World War II — Outbreak

## Beginning

World War 2 began on September 1st 1939.{depth=1}

{depth=2}
The beginning of the nearly 6-year carnage was the invasion of Poland by Nazi Germany.

{depth=3}
During the Battle of Westerplatte, circa 3400 German soldiers went against roughly 200
Polish defenders. Germans attacked with an overwhelming force consistent with the
so-called Blitzkrieg tactics. The decisive factor in German victory was air superiority
with about 60 Junkers Ju 87 dive bombers.

{depth=4}
At approximately 4:40 AM the battleship Schleswig-Holstein started firing salvos at a
Polish garrison. Shortly thereafter Major Sucharski requested backup from a Polish
military base on the Hel Peninsula. The garrison held out for 7 days before
surrendering on September 7th.

## Key Dates

| Event | Date |
|-------|------|
| German invasion of Poland | 1 Sep 1939 |
| UK and France declare war | 3 Sep 1939 |
| Soviet invasion of Poland | 17 Sep 1939 |

{depth=3}
The table above covers only the opening weeks. The war's full timeline spans nearly
6 years across multiple theatres.

## Inline depth example

The war lasted six years{depth=1}, beginning with the invasion of Poland in 1939{depth=2}, 
with Germany and the Soviet Union acting as initial co-aggressors under the 
Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact{depth=3}, a non-aggression treaty signed August 23 1939 that 
secretly partitioned Eastern Europe into spheres of influence{depth=4}.
